diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1a55755..795b558 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,7 +6,20 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": "..." | null}`: one page of
+  items ordered by `id` ascending.
+  - `limit` (optional): integer from 1 to 100, default 20. Any other value
+    (non-digits, `0`, above 100) returns 400.
+  - `cursor` (optional): the `next_cursor` value from a previous response,
+    passed back unchanged. Omit it for the first page. It is opaque; a
+    malformed value returns 400.
+  - `next_cursor` is `null` on the last page. Otherwise, request the next
+    page with `?cursor=<next_cursor>`; to read everything, keep following
+    `next_cursor` until it is `null`.
+  - Errors return `{"error": "..."}`.
+  - Breaking change for existing callers: `GET /items` without parameters
+    now returns the first 20 items, not all of them. Follow `next_cursor`
+    to read the rest.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
